Z||000018||mshill||06-18-2001||04:09 PM||||I hope this guy means "cryogenically treated" cause cybergenics has to do robots and such.  A cryogenic treatment is an extrememly low temperature hardening process for metal.  This is commonly done to alloy baseball bats in order to make them more "lively".  I think that cryogenic treatment of baseball bats has yet to be proven beneficial.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||AusFiero||06-19-2001||06:52 AM||||Originally posted by BAM-BAM:<BR><B>And here's what he said:<BR>Hey, if you want to put a "blazer" master cylinder in and pay Fiero Store prices in for their cheap junk, go ahead.</B><BR>Well rule 1 of business is don't publicly diss your competitor even if you think their stuff is junk. Most people will only hear you whining, not showing how it is better.<BR><B>The kit I sell have cybergenically treated vented rotors, and all necessary mounting hardware.</B> Yep cybergenically? Word does not exist in any dictionary I could find, it probably is cryongenically he means , wonder if he could explain the process and benefits in detail.<BR><B>$650 is not alot.</B> Might not be to him but I know US$650 is a bloody lot of money to me.<BR><B>Go ahead and add up stock Fiero <BR>brake parts.  No, I do not include a proportioning valve, you can buy it far cheaper from JC Whitney than I can offer it.</B> Well I added up my receipts and found I spent a lot less than that for new parts or reconditioned including labour and I am on the other side of the world for gods sake.<BR><B>What is cybergenically? and does it make that much of a difference? Oh well!</B><BR>I think I have the cybergenically sussed out now. Cybergenics is indeed robotics. Robots are getting intelligent. What he is trying to tell us is his brakes have minds of their own once you have them installed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><B>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
